  #block(breakable: false)[
  === Complete Solutions

  #sol-item(1, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Both sectors employ salaried staff, keep records and use equipment. The difference is public accountability, tax funding and political direction.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The permanent secretary is the administrative head and accounting officer. The minister is the political head, and the head of the civil service oversees the service as a whole.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Anonymity keeps the official out of the public argument while leaving the minister answerable to parliament. Permanence is continuity, and impartiality is equal service to any government.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The Commission appoints, promotes and disciplines. The Executive Council is the cabinet, and the National Assembly appropriates and oversees.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Udoji reviewed structure and remuneration, and the 1974 awards raised salaries and unified the grading structure.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The reform made permanent secretaries political appointees, which critics say weakened the service's neutrality. It did not abolish the commission or the service.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The TSA consolidates government cash in one account at the Central Bank, which makes leakages easier to see and reduces idle balances in commercial banks.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The recurring themes are size, cost and efficiency — Udoji, Phillips, Ayida and Oronsaye all begin from that premise.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The Auditor-General audits and reports to the legislature, which is the point of the office: it arms parliament's oversight.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Integrity is the canon that public money is not private money. Permanence and anonymity are about continuity and public profile, not honesty.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The corporation is a separate legal body created by statute, with a board and accounts. A ministry is a department of the executive, funded by appropriation.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The BPE manages the sale of state enterprises and the privatisation process. Elections, audit and tax collection belong to INEC, the Auditor-General and the FIRS.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Commercialisation imposes cost recovery without a change of ownership. Sale to private investors is privatisation.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Markets, motor parks, local roads and sanitation are local functions. Defence, passports and currency are federal.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The reform gave councils a uniform structure and functions and recognised them as a third tier.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The state government appoints caretaker committees, usually after dissolving an elected council — the clearest example of undue state control.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The statutory allocation dominates council finance, and its timing and size are decided above the council. Internal revenue is weak.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Tolls, rates, fees and licences are the council's own revenue. Company tax, import duty and royalties are federal.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The national interest is the state's own security, territorial integrity, development and prestige, which survives changes of government.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    History, geography, the economy, domestic politics and military capacity are the determinants. Party numbers, the civil service and the flag are not.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    National interest is the centre, West Africa the second circle, Africa the third and the world the fourth.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The Authority of Heads of State is supreme. The Council of Ministers, the Court and the Parliament are subordinate organs.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The AU was designed with stronger institutions for peace, security and integration, in response to the OAU's perceived weakness.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Nigeria sent troops to the UN operation in the Congo in 1960, immediately after independence; the West African operations came later.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    ECOMOG was a military deployment. The Technical Aid Corps is cultural, the embassy diplomatic and the OPEC quota economic.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The executions under Abacha led to suspension, which was lifted when Nigeria returned to civilian rule in 1999.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    OPEC coordinates production and prices through quotas. Peacekeeping, currency and interest rates belong to other institutions.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Non-alignment was a refusal of formal bloc membership while maintaining trade and diplomacy with both sides.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The embassy is the standing diplomatic machinery. Sanctions are economic, and military and cultural instruments work through other channels.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    OPEC negotiation uses a national resource as leverage, which makes it economic. The others are diplomatic, cultural and military.
  ]

  #sol-item(31, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A monocultural economy limits the resources and leverage available, which is the standard constraint in the textbooks.
  ]

  #sol-item(32, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Single-member constituencies decided by plurality. Nigeria does not use PR or the single transferable vote for the National Assembly.
  ]

  #sol-item(33, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The modified two-thirds requirement is designed to give the President a national spread, not merely a plurality.
  ]

  #sol-item(34, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Tenure and funding are the two institutional supports, with appointment through the Council of State and the Senate.
  ]

  #sol-item(35, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    State independent electoral commissions run council polls, which is why their independence from the state executive is a standing criticism.
  ]

  #sol-item(36, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    BIVAS is an accreditation technology, verifying the person. Counting is manual, and transmission is a separate function.
  ]

  #sol-item(37, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The Act conditions transmission on certified network coverage, which was the compromise that made the provision acceptable.
  ]

  #sol-item(38, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Governorship petitions go to their own tribunal, with an appeal to the Supreme Court. Only the presidential petition begins at the Court of Appeal.
  ]

  #sol-item(39, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The short filing window and the 180-day judgment limit together keep a petition from outliving the term it challenges.
  ]

  #sol-item(40, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Freedom concerns the voter's choice; an accurate register and a transparent count are conditions of fairness.
  ]

